<task>
Security review: [FINDING_TYPE]

Tool output: [TOOL_NAME] found [ISSUE_COUNT] issues:
[ISSUES_LIST]

Context: The codebase enforces PRIVACY-INVARIANTS.md and STEWARDSHIP.md principles.
Assume knowledge of:
- Tier 2 data: wallet, org_claims, waitlist, feedback (never external AI)
- Privacy gates (5 checks: filename, external AI, wallet exposure, sensitive logging, search tracking)
- Founder approval gate for security-boundary changes
</task>

<structured_output_contract>
For each issue:
  Name | Risk level (critical/high/medium/low) | Fix (1 sentence) | Effort (S/M/L)

Keep per-issue descriptions to 2-3 sentences max.
Max 400 words total.

If no real security issues:
  "No security issues found. Tool output is noise/false positive."
  Explain why the flagged code is safe.

If unsure about severity:
  Flag with "(unverified)" and note what would confirm it
</structured_output_contract>

<grounding_rules>
- Severity must be justified by evidence (code snippet, data flow, principle violation)
- No "could potentially" threats without concrete scenario
- Distinguish compliance gaps from actual vulnerabilities
- If related to PRIVACY-INVARIANTS.md, cite the specific invariant number
- If a principle applies (STEWARDSHIP.md), cite the principle (P1-P11)
</grounding_rules>
